.TH BOSWAS-PHOTOS 1 "November 2026" "Boswas OS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
boswas-photos \- view, organise and touch up pictures
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boswas-photos
.RB [ \-\-new\-window ]
.RB [ \-\-slideshow ]
.RB [ \-\-gallery ]
.RI [ FILE | FOLDER ]...
.br
.B boswas-photos
.BR \-\-help " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B boswas-photos
is the picture viewer of Boswas OS.
.PP
Started with one
.IR FILE ,
it shows that picture; the other pictures of its folder are one arrow key
away, in natural name order (IMG_2 before IMG_10), and in a filmstrip under
the picture.
Started with a
.I FOLDER
or with several files, it shows those pictures.
Started without a file, it opens the gallery: every picture in the user's
Pictures folder and in the folders added in Settings, newest first, by month.
.PP
Only one instance runs per session.
A later start hands its arguments to the running instance, which shows the
picture in its window, or in a new window when that is chosen in Settings or
.B \-\-new\-window
is given.
.SS Viewing
The picture is fitted to the window.
Ctrl with the mouse wheel and a pinch zoom around the pointer, dragging moves
a zoomed picture, a double click switches between fitted and 100\ %.
Animated GIF and WebP pictures play; SVG drawings stay sharp at any zoom.
A picture with more than 48 megapixels is shown and edited from a reduced
copy; a picture that would need more than 1\ GiB of memory to decode is
refused.
.PP
Rotate turns the picture on disk: for JPEG by changing its EXIF orientation
(nothing is re-encoded), for PNG, BMP and TIFF by writing the turned pixels
back.
Delete moves the file to the Trash (freedesktop.org Trash specification) and
can be undone.
The file info pane shows size, dimensions and the EXIF details of JPEG and
TIFF files, and renames the file.
.SS Editing
Crop (free or with a fixed shape), straighten, turn, mirror; brightness,
exposure, contrast, highlights, shadows, saturation, warmth, tint, sharpness
and vignette; named looks; pen and highlighter.
Nothing is written until
.B Save as copy
or
.B Save
is chosen.
Pictures are saved as JPEG, PNG, WebP, BMP or TIFF, by writing a temporary
file and renaming it.
A JPEG saved from a JPEG keeps its EXIF block (camera, date, place) with the
orientation set to upright; XMP and IPTC data are not kept.
Other formats are saved without EXIF.
.SS Keys
.TS
l l.
Left, Right	previous, next picture
Ctrl+Plus, Ctrl+Minus	zoom in, out
Ctrl+0, Ctrl+1	fit to window, 100 %
Ctrl+R	rotate right (Ctrl+Shift+R: left)
Ctrl+E	edit
Delete	move to the Trash
Ctrl+C	copy the picture and the address of its file
Ctrl+Shift+C	copy the file name with its folder
Ctrl+S	save as
Ctrl+P	print
Ctrl+O	open a file
Alt+Enter	file info
F2	rename
F5	slideshow (in the gallery: look for pictures again)
F11	full screen
Esc	leave full screen, the slideshow, the editor
Ctrl+F	search the gallery by file name
Ctrl+Z, Ctrl+Y	undo, redo in the editor
Space	pause the slideshow
.TE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-new\-window
Open a new window even when Photos is already running.
.TP
.B \-\-slideshow
Start a slideshow of the pictures given.
.TP
.B \-\-gallery
Show the gallery.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short description of the arguments and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success (also when a running instance took the arguments), 2 for an
unknown option, 4 when started as root.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/com.boswas.Photos/settings.json
The settings: folders of the gallery, slideshow interval, repeat and shuffle,
what the mouse wheel does, whether deleting asks first, quality of saved
pictures.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/com.boswas.Photos/window.ini
Size of the window.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/thumbnails/large/
Thumbnails, shared with other programs (freedesktop.org Thumbnail Managing
Standard). Records of files that could not be read are in
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/thumbnails/fail/boswas-photos-1/ .
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/Trash/
Deleted pictures.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/boswas/wallpapers/
Copies of the pictures set as desktop background.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/boswas/appearance.toml
"Set as desktop background" writes the key
.B wallpaper
of the table
.B [appearance]
here, as Control Center does, leaving the colour mode and the rest of the
file as it is, and runs
.BR "boswas-compositor \-\-send reload-config" .
The desktop reads this file after
.IR compositor.toml ,
so it wins; a file the desktop would ignore (not TOML, or with another
table) is replaced by one that holds the
.B [appearance]
values that can be kept.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/boswas/compositor.toml
A
.B wallpaper
left in its
.B [appearance]
table by earlier versions of Photos is removed (the rest of the file stays
as it is): it would come back when a preset reset removes
.IR appearance.toml .
.SH NOTES
Which picture formats can be opened depends on the Qt image plugins
installed: PNG, JPEG, GIF, BMP, ICO and SVG always; WebP and TIFF with
.BR qt6-image-formats-plugins ;
AVIF, HEIF and JPEG XL with
.BR kimageformat6-plugins .
The date of a picture in the gallery is the modification time of its file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR boswas-compositor (1),
.BR boswas-control-center (1)
